This is not a claim that one stage causes the next across kingdoms. It is a claim that the same operational logic—activation, stabilization, allocation, and maintenance—recurs across independently studied systems.
That is a legitimate and useful form of cross-domain pattern recognition. Scientific analogies are most valuable when they organize relations among components and generate testable questions rather than merely assert resemblance.

